    "available_at": "2026-10-23T21:06:52.586549+00:00",
    "body": "Drewry’s World Container Index rose 2% to $4,585 per 40-foot container, supported by higher rates on trans-Pacific and Asia-Europe routes as strong U.S. import demand and carrier capacity cuts bolstered pricing.\nShanghai-to-Los Angeles rates increased 2% to $8,007 per 40-foot container, while Shanghai-to-New York rates edged up 1% to $10,166. Drewry expects trans-Pacific rates to remain stable next week, with U.S. import demand continuing to support the market despite an increase in available capacity.\nCarriers have announced only two blank sailings on the trans-Pacific for next week, down from six this week, according to figures from Drewry’s Container Capacity Insight. The service tracks scheduled and canceled sailings, effective capacity and port congestion across major trade lanes.\nRates from Shanghai to Rotterdam rose 3% to $3,632 per 40-foot container, while Shanghai-to-Genoa rates increased 5% to $4,152.\nUnlike the trans-Pacific, the Asia-Europe trade faces more sailing cancellations next week. Carriers have announced eight blank sailings, up from two this week, tightening available capacity as they seek to put upward pressure on freight rates.\nDrewry expects Asia-Europe rates to increase slightly next week as capacity reductions support pricing.\nThe cuts come as congestion at key Asian ports eases. Vessel waiting times at Shanghai fell from 97 hours in Week 38 to 38 hours in Week 42, signaling a substantial improvement in port operations.\nSecurity risks and attacks on ships continue to affect vessel movements through the Persian Gulf. Only two containerships sailed into the Gulf in Week 42, down from five the previous week. Meanwhile, sailings through the Suez Canal increased slightly, from 54 in Week 41 to 55 in Week 42.\nWhy it matters: The increase signals continued cost pressure on importers, even as congestion at major Asian ports eases. Strong U.S. demand is supporting trans-Pacific rates, while Asia–Europe carriers are canceling more sailings to tighten available space and bolster pricing, leaving shippers’ costs dependent on both cargo demand and carrier capacity decisions.\nRead more articles by Stuart Chirls here .\nRead more: Russian diesel tanker heads for U.S. following Trump-Putin deal\nTime-definite ocean delivery? Container ship completes new Arctic route trial\nHow new capacity is raising rates in chaotic ocean market\nNo. 2 container line studying US-UK route for nuclear ships\nTrans-Pacific facing new booking risks as reliability sinks\nUpcoming FreightWaves Events\nCompliance\nBrokerage Compliance Symposium\nThe day before F3. Every compliance issue you face - fraud exposure, carrier liability, FMCSA rules, cargo theft, insurance gaps - navigated by attorneys and operators defining best practices in a changing industry.\nOctober 26, 2026\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nRegister Now\nAwards\nF3 Awards Dinner\nThe night before F3. FreightTech100 companies honored. FreightTech 25 and Shipper of Choice winners revealed live. Cocktail reception into dinner and live music - 300 industry leaders in one purpose-built room.\nOctober 26, 2026\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nRegister Now\nFreightTech\nF3: Future of Freight Festival\nIndustry-defining keynotes, rapid-fire technology demos, and industry leaders networking in experiences across Chattanooga - plus the inaugural F3 Awards Dinner featuring the FreightTech and Shipper of Choice reveals.\nOctober 27, 2026 – October 28, 2026\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nRegister Now\nCompliance Brokerage Compliance Symposium Oct 26 • The Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nThe day before F3. Every compliance issue you face - fraud exposure, carrier liability, FMCSA rules, cargo theft, insurance gaps - navigated by attorneys and operators defining best practices in a changing industry.\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN Register Now\nAwards F3 Awards Dinner Oct 26 • The Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nThe night before F3. FreightTech100 companies honored. FreightTech 25 and Shipper of Choice winners revealed live. Cocktail reception into dinner and live music - 300 industry leaders in one purpose-built room.\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN Register Now\nFreightTech F3: Future of Freight Festival Oct 27 – Oct 28 • The Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nIndustry-defining keynotes, rapid-fire technology demos, and industry leaders networking in experiences across Chattanooga - plus the inaugural F3 Awards Dinner featuring the FreightTech and Shipper of Choice reveals.\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN Register Now",
